MENTOR: So Door turns from the middle of its left edge. Right now, Door's pivot is at its center.

Here's the idea behind this. **Anchor Point is where the pivot sits inside the layer, and Position is where that pivot sits in the comp.** If you change Anchor Point alone, the layer slides so the new pivot lands where the old one was. Pan Behind changes both together, so nothing moves on screen.

(I also tried to grab a frame of Door at 0 s, but it came back as a single pixel, so there's nothing useful to show from it.)

